															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drsekora" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6398764); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6398764&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606056698" alt="DrSekora" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6398764)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drsekora" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6398764); return false;" >DrSekora</a></span> <span class="odate time_1602291006 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">10 Oct 2020 00:50</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4792455">
									

<p>Some more non-professional crit! (Saw you post this in the IRC, was intrigued.)</p>
<p>Overall, I like the concept, and the execution is pretty solid. I have mostly nitpicks and minor suggestions, aside from being a little unconvinced about the scale - people seem to care too much about this thing, which I get is sort of the point but it stretches believability (especially given how other &quot;this SCP appeared on Site-XX one day&quot; scenarios are often handled).</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Conprocs</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Unnecessary phrase:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It should not be held within <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">a minimum of</span> 10 meters of any other anomalous objects.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Comma needed (or restructure, e.g. omit the first comma):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>personnel, including the Site Director assigned to Secure Site 73<span style="color: blue">,</span> must be</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Description</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Consider indicating that the object is a rock somewhere in the description - I don't think the average reader (even the average Foundation reader) is going to know what a Banded Carnelian is (you could maybe get away with a footnote). I thought it was an egg for quite a while.</p>
<p>I think it would make more sense to use volume instead of area here, unless you intend the effect to extend &quot;infinitely&quot; upwards (or for the Foundation to not have done testing in that dimension, but that seems unlikely given the context). Speaking of size, also consider giving some indication of the size of the object - is it tiny, does it fit snugly in your hand, or does it take some effort to lift?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">First&nbsp;Part&nbsp;of&nbsp;Addendum</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>&quot;Foundation&quot; should be capitalized in the first sentence.</p>
<p>Consider changing phrasing to something like &quot;The discovery of such an object&quot;, to avoid repetition:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The discovery of an unrecorded anomalous object</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So here, we have a Senior Researcher being yanked off his current project(s) and being given a bevy of resources (12 underlings, unlimited(?!) funding, some high-level clearances, and fast-pass access to RAISA), in an email that CC's every O5 member. I get that you're trying to emphasize that the Foundation leadership thinks this is important, but this seems a bit over-the-top</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">First&nbsp;addenda&nbsp;collapsible&nbsp;(preliminary)</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Is the first message from Max Schmitz or Laura Harris?</p>
<p>Consider adding <tt>hideLocation=&quot;both&quot;</tt> for convenience to your collapsibles, since they're longish.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Second&nbsp;addenda&nbsp;collapsible&nbsp;(documentation)</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I don't think it makes sense to conclude that the object must have been inserted after construction finished - it could have just as easily been inserted during construction (a time when there are workers coming and going) without being marked on the floorplan. Consider supplementing with something like photographic evidence dated to shortly after construction finished.</p>
<p>One of your footnotes in the Funding form is missing a bracket, so it's rendered in-line.</p>
<p>Odd that RAISA wouldn't grant Okamura access, despite earlier indications that he had been given all sorts of special privileges. Good job putting in something that sticks out, then gets explained by the reveal at the end.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Final&nbsp;collapsible&nbsp;(secret&nbsp;stuff)</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Ok, if I'm reading this right, it looks like the proposal is about faking the documentation found by Okamura at the end of the previous collapsible? If so, that's a nice twist, but it took a couple readings to catch the dates. I could just be tired, but it seems a little subtle for what seems like it should be a big reveal. Might be a necessary evil, but maybe you could emphasize the dates a bit more, or use the ethics committee meeting to drop a larger hint in case a reader misses it earlier.</p>
<p>Smaller stuff:</p>
<ul>
<li>There are some more uncapitalized &quot;foundation&quot;s throughout.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>In the proposal, there's an &quot;it's&quot; that should be &quot;its&quot;:</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>Due to it's threat to the Foundation's operation</p>
</blockquote>
<ul>
<li>This is a confusing phrase, I think it might be syntactically valid but consider reworking for clarity:</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>evidence in favour of an accurate timeline for the investigation into the origins of SCP-XXXX is to be created</p>
</blockquote>
<p>(I assume you're trying to say roughly &quot;[evidence supporting [the SCP being inserted within a specific window]] should be falsified and given to [the investigation into [the origins of SCP-XXXX]]&quot;.)</p>
<ul>
<li>This part doesn't work syntactically with the sentence it belongs to, so you'll want to rephrase:</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>rather than the best interests of the Foundation.</p>
</blockquote>
<ul>
<li>It's unclear why the ethics council vote is redacted - are we meant to speculate that the evidence found by Okamura may actually be legitimate? Or that the O5 disregarded an ethics committee vote? I'm not sure this adds meaningfully to the article, but I'd get more opinions on it because it might be a personal preference.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>

