<p>Thank you so much for the crit :)</p>
<p>All the little stuff like spag and syntax you've pointed out as a second set of eyes has been a massive help and I'm going through and editing right now. I've scaled down the e-mail quite a bit because reading it the next day I think you're totally right that it's unnecessary. Names have been cleaned up and I'm rewording stuff as I go.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">The&nbsp;ending&nbsp;</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>On the ending, you might be right that it is too subtle - originally, the last email where the funding form was found was written the day after the O5 vote, but I thought the idea of a little ambiguity in the ending rather than damn near proof that the O5 falsified the files might be a more lasting ending.</p>
<p>The intention was to try and convey that the evidence might be legitimate, and I'll brainstorm on how to get that across better tonight. For now, I'll leave the ending as is other than a bit of clean up but if many people echo your sentiments I may just roll it back to without the EC section and more clear proof that the documents are edited.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Thanks so much again for the detailed crit, you've been a massive help in getting this to a readable state.</p>

