<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Was asked to take a look at this. Expect crit within 24 hours.</span></p>
<p>Yes, this is very snappy. The prose and the writing are all generally tight in a way I can really enjoy, barring the occasional absented space or &quot;SCP-XXX&quot;.</p>
<p>I think that my biggest issue with the draft is just the fact that the object is wholy mundane, which makes justifying the ensuing O5 involvement and Ethics Committee involvement difficult. The object in question is just Procrastinati or any other antimeme, and not a particularly effective one at that. I think I'd care more about the story if there were some element about the rock that was intriguing/unexplained on its own, or presented some (perhaps negligible) threat. There's also the concern that there's no real satisfying or implied conclusion for this thing's origins — perhaps, again, due to the mundanity of its effect.</p>
<p>There's also just&#8230; something about that image. I don't know. I've never been a fan of pictures with totally white backgrounds — it feels very inauthentic.</p>
<p>To address your concerns in the top post — everything seems to stay its welcome pretty well, barring the one section listing off the previous owners. I feel like the candidate list could be downsized somewhat.</p>

							</div>

								
